{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/alternate","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/cue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/editorial","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/ossia","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/regular"],"title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The staff-type value can be ossia, editorial, cue, alternate, or regular. An ossia staff represents music","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that can be played instead of what appears on the regular staff. An editorial staff also represents musical","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alternatives, but is created by an editor rather than the composer. It can be used for suggested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpretations or alternatives from other sources. A cue staff represents music from another part. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alternate staff shares the same music as the prior staff, but displayed differently (e.g., treble and bass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clef, standard notation and tablature). It is not included in playback. An alternate staff provides more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"information to an application reading a file than encoding the sa